abstract: >-
  Localized linear excitations of a complex scalar Q-ball in three spatial
  dimensions with potential U(S) = S - S^2 + S^3/2. Computer-assisted existence
  arguments (interval arithmetic plus analytic exterior estimates) for two
  radial modes and one dipole mode on the infinite radial domain; a numerical
  radial sequence with candidates up to index eighteen; a thin-wall
  phase-matching interpretation with an unfitted planar spacing candidate; and a
  conditional second-harmonic obstruction to a specified localized nonlinear
  continuation. Preprint, not peer reviewed. Produced with extensive use of AI
  tools (Claude, Anthropic; Codex, OpenAI) under the author's direction.
keywords:
  - Q-ball
  - bound state in the continuum
  - interval arithmetic
  - computer-assisted proof
